From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:36:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wordcraft-aros: break the rasterizer and the repaint schedule
 down in WORDCRAFT_PERF

Problem: run wp1 showed the GUI rasterizer taking 94-99 % of every frame
  and the loop never sleeping, but not which part of paint costs what, nor
  what asks for the repaints.
Rationale: with WORDCRAFT_PERF, paint counts per kind of triangle (user
  texture such as the page image; solid fills, which sample the atlas's
  white texel; atlas text) the triangles, visited and covered pixels,
  bilinear and nearest samples, blended and opaque writes, and times runs of
  consecutive same-kind triangles (two clock reads per run, none per pixel);
  clear is timed alone. The loop records the timeout it slept with, whether
  an event or the timeout woke it, how late the due repaint was, the delay
  egui asked for next, and egui's repaint causes (file:line reason) per
  segment, written to <file>.causes.csv.
Scope: diagnostic; without WORDCRAFT_PERF the pixel loop keeps four local
  counters and nothing else changes.
Upstream-status: local-only.
Verification: see the port's evidence reports (run wp2).
Removal: with 0008.
